From: MilkFlint <milkflint@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: read the scan request before
 ieee80211_start_roc_work() uses it

350-mac80211-allow-scanning-while-on-radar-channel.patch added a
ieee80211_can_leave_ch() check at the start of ieee80211_start_roc_work()
that passes the scan request, which the function reads only further down:
the check got an uninitialised pointer. ieee80211_is_radar_required()
dereferences it when an interface on the radio needs radar detection, so
a remain-on-channel or off-channel management frame on a DFS channel
could oops.

Read it before the check.

---
--- a/net/mac80211/offchannel.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/offchannel.c
@@ -619,6 +619,7 @@ static int ieee80211_start_roc_work(struct ieee80211_l
 
 	cfg80211_chandef_create(&chandef, channel, NL80211_CHAN_NO_HT);
 	radio_mask = ieee80211_chandef_radio_mask(local, &chandef);
+	req = wiphy_dereference(local->hw.wiphy, local->scan_req);
 	if (!ieee80211_can_leave_ch(sdata, req, radio_mask) &&
 	    !ieee80211_scanning_busy(local, &chandef))
 		return -EBUSY;
@@ -657,8 +658,6 @@ static int ieee80211_start_roc_work(struct ieee80211_l
 		roc->mgmt_tx_cookie = *cookie;
 	}
 
-	req = wiphy_dereference(local->hw.wiphy, local->scan_req);
-
 	/* if there's no need to queue, handle it immediately */
 	if (list_empty(&local->roc_list) && !local->scanning) {
 		/* if not HW assist, just queue & schedule work */
